    "description": "<table style=\"width:100%; margin-top:2em; border:2px solid #999; font-size:105%; text-align:center; background:#00008B;\"> \n <tbody>\n  <tr> \n   <td><i><b>This <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Homebrew_Content\" title=\"Homebrew Content\">Homebrew Content</a> has been <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Category:Tested\" title=\"Category:Tested\">Tested</a> per the <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Category:Untested\" title=\"Category:Untested\">Untested</a> guidelines. Whether or not it can be used is, as always, the prerogative of the Gamemaster.</b></i> </td>\n  </tr>\n </tbody>\n</table><p><i>Vibroarbir Blade weapon data created by Wikia user Chellewalker (formally Wikia user Lukewarner).</i> </p><p>One pair of Snoke's Praetorian Guards wields twin Vibroarbir Blades that can be joined at the ends to form a single double-bladed polearm or wielded independently in each hand. The blades' metal edges are complemented by razor-sharp beams of electro-plasma. </p><p>As a <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Swift_Action\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Swift Action\">Swift Action</a>, you can combine two Vibroarbir Blades, at which point they become a Double Weapon statistically equivalent to a <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Double_Vibroblade\" title=\"Double Vibroblade\">Double Vibroblade</a>. After doing so, you can attack with both ends of the weapon as a <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Full-Round_Action\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Full-Round Action\">Full-Round Action</a>, but both attack rolls take a -10 penalty (although certain <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Feats\" title=\"Feats\">Feats</a> and <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Talents\" title=\"Talents\">Talents</a> can reduce these penalties). </p><p>A Vibroarbir Blade requires an <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Energy_Cell\" title=\"Energy Cell\">Energy Cell</a> to operate. </p>",
